Reconfirm the revised complete RFC-257 WS-D DESIGN (v12), not implementation. Repo /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go. Candidate TREE 5a28ecbc718291b8bad5510867c375acfcdff246; design rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-d-design.md SHA256 1bd420cd5fedce7309fc766d40408a04f9ddcc7476d078d03b9ec6658993b018 (1644 lines). Previous: v11 TREE 01b0669d8d12e6eb84eebfa31f160cfed853e5d5 (four NAKs, rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-d-design-review-v11/*.txt); earlier rounds in -v1..-v10. Accepted WS-C source TREE f0cb29576cde624e0f1c6e22ca18a5180d1b298f. Test-run tree 65d3ffba83b3eda56e3d97430fbd49bb3ff6b9ca (the gate tree adds only README item 28's just-test paragraph).
Delta since v11 touching WS-D: (1) phase D-0 rebuilt (section 5 'Attempt bounds of the transaction owners', Decision v12 and Fixtures): every attempt goes through d.transactor with the client loop capped at one attempt (retry limit 0), runOnce moved onto that route, one attemptLoop with fdb.IsRetryable and the ported ExponentialDelay serving Run/RunWithVersionstamp/RunWithWeakReads (weak reads on attempt 1 only)/RunRead/RunWithRetry/cleanupHeartbeatWithin; a per-owner policy from a caller census (online indexer: its own SetMaxAttempts; SQL autocommit and DDL: ONE attempt as the target's relational layer; SQL page reads, statistics, fleet, CLI, chaos: database default; SPFresh: unchanged on its own unbounded client loop, recorded in RFC-094 section 2); terminal-caller handling incl. shouldLessenWork; both client backends; a new chaos fault FaultRetryable (no commit) and a non-zero injected-fault guard on every faulting scenario; a --runs_per_test census plus attempt histograms instead of one suite run; LastStep MERGE for the merger fixture and in GuardiANN phase 4; (2) peel admission: W now carries the KMeans knobs (I*(R+1)/32), B lowered from 4e7 to 2.5e7, evaluated after Step 1's preconditions; new measurement (oracle item 26, spec 'measures the unsampled floor peel in the admitted high-dimension corner', 6 pinned rows at n=1001 d=2048/2775 and n=2000 d=1250): smaller child 0.376-0.495, worst refit 8.0e-8 s per n*d so <=2.0 s at the bound; balance/timing/replica-volume/2101 statements corrected; Go-side calibration rule for B; knob-factor fixture; reconcile latency stated; (3) PRODUCTION FIX (landed with pins): Go's ongoing-build check evaluates the heartbeat population Java's getIndexingHeartbeats map leaves (a (U) and a (U,x) key collapse to the later value; pkg/recordlayer/indexing_heartbeat_admin.go collectIndexingHeartbeats), Go spec and JVM spec pin both pairs, keep-first mutation reddens both (item 27); JVM spec also pins the 'Versionstamp cannot be cast' message; DIVERGENCES entry updated; (4) README items 23/25 corrected (capture run, cache provenance), items 26-28; evidence-run.txt regenerated from two uncached 27/27 runs. NOT WS-D, same tree, own gates: WS-E v4 (in progress), WS-F v2 verdicts, WS-J v2 verdicts (their files and review directories are in the tree).
Run records: /var/tmp/fdb-upgrade-recovery/rfc257-v12-1.log and -2.log (oracle, uncached), wsd-corner-1.log (item 26 capture), hb-v12*.log (item 27 incl. mutations), just-test-v12.log with manifests wsd-v12-manifest-before/after.txt (README item 28).
