Read ALL four v11 verdicts, the FULL v12 design and its diff from v11, RFC-094's new section 2 paragraph, the oracle README and evidence, the oracle source/test, and check claims against actual Java and current Go. Challenge sufficiency and interactions with the rest of the design (especially D-0's per-owner policies, the transactor route and chaos fault semantics, SQL autocommit single attempt, and the admission rule), not only whether the requested words appear. Distinguish measured target facts from remaining source hypotheses.
Preserved boundaries: GuardiANN executes in merger-supplied transactions (no invented child runner); SPFresh independent algorithms/LIRE; approved raw/nullable-array/scalar/sort extensions; C++ 7.3.77 (the raw pure-Go client keeps libfdb_c's unbounded default); format max 15/default 14; Lucene is separate upgrade-wide work, not Go TEXT; WS-D cannot complete with a refusal or fake backend.
